; THREE HIDDEN BUFFS, ONE APPLICATOR, AND THE COUNT IS NOT ARBITRARY. Buff.trigger_timing is a single
; @export that ReactionBus.does_buff_trigger compares directly (reaction_bus.gd:135), so the
; bookkeeping subscribes at POST. The other two are a different kind: they name no trigger at all,
; because Buff.TO.ACTION_FORBIDDEN and Buff.TO.ACTION_PER_ROUND are channels the engine QUERIES rather
; than ones the bus fires, and each buff has exactly one `to`.
;
;   buff_symbiosis            POST  stamps the round's extra as spent, caps the refill, clears on new round
;   buff_symbiosis_exclusion  -     hides (ACTION_FORBIDDEN) a 1/scene or 1/mission reaction as the extra
;   buff_symbiosis_extra_use  -     +1 to a reaction's per-round hard limit while the extra is unspent
;
; THE THIRD IS SP2.5 TASK 1, and it exists because the first two only ever reached ONE of the two
; gates a reaction can be refused by. They live in the reaction-POINT economy (is_gear_affordable,
; unit_action.gd:182), which never refuses a reaction with consumes_rxn = false - so the Uffish Gyre's
; and Halo's 1/round, which is the OTHER gate (is_under_per_round_limit, unit_action.gd:170-175), was
; untouched by the trait and a second one was never offered. See buff_symbiosis_extra_use.gd.
;
; ONE PassiveBuffApplicator carries all three deliberately: the exclusion reads the bookkeeping's
; SPENT_KEY and so does the extra use, so "either all three are on the unit or none are" is what
; keeps those reads from having to handle a half-applied trait.
;
; reapply_at_the_start_of_each_turn IS STILL UNSET, and the third buff does not change that. A
; re-application hands over fresh BuffCores and would wipe the stamp mid-round;
; test_the_myconids_own_turn_start_also_caps_once_the_extra_is_spent is what falsifies setting it.
[sub_resource type="Resource" id="Resource_applicator"]
script = ExtResource("5_applicator")
applied_buffs = Array[ExtResource("6_buff")]([ExtResource("7_bookkeeping"), ExtResource("8_exclusion"), ExtResource("9_extra_use")])

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_kit")
passives = Array[ExtResource("2_passive")]([SubResource("Resource_statincrease"), SubResource("Resource_applicator")])
is_trait = true
icon_override = ExtResource("10_icon")
